        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.085,
            0.899,
            0.117
          ],
          "content": "**On applying Ohm’s law to the three resistors separately, we further have**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.367,
            0.117,
            0.896,
            0.136
          ],
          "content": "V _ { _ { \\cal I } } = { \\cal I }   R _ { _ { \\cal I } }\\tag{[11.13(a)]}",
          "image_source": "images/page_13_equation_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.367,
            0.138,
            0.896,
            0.157
          ],
          "content": "V _ { _ 2 } = I   R _ { _ 2 }\\tag{[11.13(b)]}",
          "image_source": "images/page_13_equation_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.16,
            0.455,
            0.178
          ],
          "content": "**and** $V _ { _ 3 } = I   R _ { _ 3 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.811,
            0.159,
            0.897,
            0.176
          ],
          "content": "**[11.13(c)]**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.183,
            0.468,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": "**From Eq. (11.11),**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.366,
            0.204,
            0.546,
            0.222
          ],
          "content": "IR = IR_{1} + IR_{2} + IR_{3}",
          "image_source": "images/page_13_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.222,
            0.335,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": "**or**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.366,
            0.235,
            0.897,
            0.254
          ],
          "content": "R_{s}=R_{l}+R_{2}+R_{3}\\tag{11.14}",
          "image_source": "images/page_13_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.276,
            0.259,
            0.899,
            0.31
          ],
          "content": "**We can conclude that when several resistors are joined in series, the** resistance of the combination $R _ { s }$ **equals the sum of their individual** resistances**,** $R _ { \\iota } , R _ { \\iota ^ { \\prime } } R _ { \\substack { 3 ^ { \\prime } } }$ **and is thus greater than any individual resistance.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.318,
            0.454,
            0.333
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Example 11.7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.334,
            0.899,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": "**An electric lamp, whose resistance is 20** Ω**, and a conductor of 4** Ω **resistance are connected to a 6 V battery (Fig. 11.9). Calculate (a) the total resistance of the circuit, (b) the current through the circuit, and (c) the potential difference across the electric lamp and conductor.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.269,
            0.409,
            0.712,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.273,
                0.639,
                0.702,
                0.668
              ],
              "content": "Figure 11.9 An electric lamp connected in series with a resistor of 4 Ω to a 6 V battery"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.676,
            0.401,
            0.691
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Solution"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.693,
            0.677,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": "The resistance of electric lamp, $R _ { \\iota }   = 2 0 \\: \\Omega$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.708,
            0.844,
            0.725
          ],
          "content": "The resistance of the conductor connected in series, $R _ {   _ { 2 } }   = 4 \\; \\Omega .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.725,
            0.647,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": "**Then the total resistance in the circuit**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.744,
            0.425,
            0.76
          ],
          "content": "R_{ 滘 } = R_{_l} + R_{_2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_13_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.761,
            0.522,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": "R_{_s} = 20 \\; \\Omega + 4 \\; \\Omega = 24 \\; \\Omega.",
          "image_source": "images/page_13_equation_19.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.78,
            0.898,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": "**The total potential difference across the two terminals of the battery** $V   = 6 \\; \\mathrm { V } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.816,
            0.854,
            0.833
          ],
          "content": "**Now by Ohm’s law, the current through the circuit is given by**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.835,
            0.446,
            0.882
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{array} { r c l } { { I } } & { { = } } & { { V / R _ { \\mathrm { s } } } } \\\\ { { } } & { { = } } & { { 6   \\mathrm { V } / 2 4   \\Omega } } \\\\ { { } } & { { = } } & { { 0 . 2 5   \\mathrm { A } . } } \\end{array}",
          "image_source": "images/page_13_equation_22.jpg"
        },
